Z||000000||Steve Normington||06-05-2001||04:36 PM||||Its been so long since the car was disassembled that my ID tags have faded to unreadability. I have two sets of wires that are near the starter. Each set has two wires connected to a single terminal. (4 wires, two terminals, two wires per terminal). Any idea where these connect. I assume one connects to the constant hot on the starter, but which one, and where does the other one go. The manual is no help because it doesn't tell you where the wires physical connection is. I keep forgetting to note the color codes when I'm under there.<P>------------------<BR>I don't car if my next Fiero is a 2M Hamster, I'm not swapping the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bill 88||06-05-2001||05:34 PM||||The hot wire from the battery goes to the large starter lug the small connector with two wires goes to the starter energize terminal on the starter.  I 'believe' that the other wire with the large lug is a 'GROUND' and goes to the ground stud on the block near the starter.  I chased that problem on my 88 for three weeks.  But I am new so I could be wrong.  Let me know what you find out.||||reg||1
